cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Autonometry, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: Autonometry
abstract: >-
  Autonometry measures how much of a robot's work is done by its AI and how much by humans,
  local or remote. It records every change of control in a sealed, tamper-evident log, verifies
  logs, reconciles a robot's log with a teleoperation station's log, and reports autonomy
  metrics with confidence intervals. It is the reference implementation of an open
  specification.
authors:
  - given-names: Aaryan
    family-names: Solanki
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Autonometry/autonometry"
url: "https://github.com/Autonometry/autonometry"
keywords:
  - robotics
  - autonomy
  - teleoperation
  - audit log
  - metrics
